=== ★★★★★ THE BEACON — DID THE WHOLE GUEST STOP, OR ONLY A PROCESS? ===
    beacon samples captured = [358]   (⊘ 0 ⇒ THE BEACON NEVER RAN; every reading below is VACUOUS, not zero)
      GAP    1.388 s  at epoch 1786701320.722 (sample 40)
      GAP    1.361 s  at epoch 1786701368.794 (sample 218)
    max inter-sample gap = 1.388 s   (nominal 0.25 s)
    gaps > 1.0 s         = 2
    beacon span          = 96.2 s

    ★★★ HOW TO READ THIS, pre-registered so neither answer can be the favourable one:
      • a stalled cup3 WITH beacon gaps of the same order ⇒ GLOBAL freeze — consistent
        with the BQL mechanism (doorbell handler holds the BQL; all vCPUs + main loop stop).
      • a stalled cup3 with the beacon TICKING THROUGHOUT ⇒ a PER-PROCESS wait; the BQL
        hypothesis is REFUTED for this shape and the wait is on a lock/completion.
      • both processes green + no gaps ⇒ inline is fine AT THIS WORK SIZE. ⊘ That is a
        real result: the hazard would be LATENT, arriving when CE work is forwarded to a
        real engine and the inline span grows.

